# Windows SDK requirements that a servicing REVISION decides, not the version.
#
# The SDK's directories and registry keys are named after the major build --
# "10.0.26100.0" -- and carry no servicing revision at all. So
# Include/10.0.26100.0/um existing is a true statement that answers nothing:
# revision 4654 and revision 7705 are indistinguishable by presence. That is
# how the sixth Windows defect got through a preflight that checks every
# prerequisite directory. This file is the revision axis, asserted separately.
#
# Three whitespace-separated columns. Lines starting with # are comments.
# "<version>" in a path is replaced with build/WINDOWS_SDK_VERSION.
#
#   symbol  <directory>  <identifier>
#       The identifier must appear in some .h file under that directory. Used
#       where the revision is legible only from the headers' contents, which is
#       the normal case: headers carry no version resource.
#
#   version <file>  <minimum>
#       The file's FileVersion must be >= the minimum, compared as a dotted
#       version. Used where a real version resource exists.
#
# SOURCES
#
# .workspace/src/docs/windows_build_instructions.md:54-56 requires
#   "[Windows 11 SDK] version 10.0.26100.7705", and build/WINDOWS_SDK_INSTALLER_*
#   pins that exact release. Chromium names a revision, not a floor, and the
#   pin travels with build/CHROMIUM_VERSION.
#
# .workspace/src/docs/windows_build_instructions.md:57-59 requires
#   "(Windows 11) SDK Debugging Tools 10.0.26100.3323 or higher. This version of
#   the Debugging tools is needed in order to support reading the large-page
#   PDBs that Chrome uses to allow greater-than 4 GiB PDBs." That one IS a
#   floor, and dbghelp.dll carries a version resource, so it is checked
#   numerically rather than by symbol.
#
# IUIAutomationClientInfoSource and IUIAutomationClientInfo are used
#   unconditionally by ui/accessibility/platform/uia_client_info_source_win.cc
#   (lines 24, 30, 56, 66) with no preprocessor guard and no __has_include, so
#   an older 26100 revision is a hard compile error rather than a silently
#   disabled feature. Measured: the windows-x64 gate reached 26,642 of 33,797
#   edges on SDK 10.0.26100.4654 and failed with
#   "error: unknown type name 'IUIAutomationClientInfo'".
#
# EXPERIMENTAL_IDCompositionDevice6 is used unconditionally by
#   ui/gl/direct_composition_support.cc:788, ui/gl/dc_layer_tree.cc:147 and
#   ui/gl/dc_layer_tree.h:486, with no guard, and is declared nowhere in the
#   checkout -- searched ui, gpu, media, base, build and
#   third_party/win_build_output for a declaration and found none -- so it comes
#   from the SDK's dcomp.h. Microsoft ships experimental DirectComposition
#   interfaces under that prefix and adds them in servicing revisions. Unlike
#   the UIA row this one has not been observed failing: the series gate may not
#   reach ui/gl/direct_composition_support.cc, but a full Windows build does.
#   It is asserted because the dependency is real and asserting it is free, not
#   because a run has proved it missing.
#
# IDCompositionDevice2, IDCompositionDevice3 and IDCompositionDevice4 are used
#   unconditionally in the same files and are NOT listed: all three predate
#   26100, and build/vs_toolchain.py only bothers checking for
#   IDCompositionDevice4 when the SDK's major build is <= 22621.
#
# ADDING A ROW
#
# A row belongs here when a build input's adequacy depends on an SDK servicing
# revision and presence cannot tell you. Cite the consumer and, if it exists,
# the run that found it. Prefer a `version` row when a version resource exists,
# because a number that can be compared beats a symbol that has to be chosen.
#
# The list cannot be completed by reading. An unconditional use of a too-new
# interface is a compile error in whichever translation unit uses it, so the
# authoritative enumeration is a build, not a search. What this file buys is
# that each one is found once and then asserted in seconds forever.

symbol	Include/<version>/um	IUIAutomationClientInfoSource
symbol	Include/<version>/um	IUIAutomationClientInfo
symbol	Include/<version>/um	EXPERIMENTAL_IDCompositionDevice6
version	Debuggers/x64/dbghelp.dll	10.0.26100.3323
